*.run/
*.run.md
.temp/

# Benchmark inputs are regenerated deterministically by each pattern's
# inputs/gen.py (.memory/02-bench-rules.md); gen.py is committed, blobs are not.
patterns/*/inputs/*.bin
patterns-php/*/inputs/*.bin

__pycache__/
*.pyc

*.zip
*.tar.gz

# Diagnostic gate runs. `--skip`, `--no-build`, `--no-callgrind` and `--cells
# measured` all certify strictly less than a full run, so check.py writes them
# beside the full-run record rather than over it. Only the full-run record is
# committed evidence.
results/gate/*.partial.json
results-php/gate/*.partial.json

# `harness-php/gate.py --preflight` writes one of these per invocation. It
# carries a `when` timestamp and the literal `gate_argv`, so it churns on every
# run -- measured, two consecutive identical-source runs differ. The GENERATOR is
# committed and the artefact is not, the same rule as `.temp/` and the input
# blobs. ⚠ It is also the only place `harness_php_sha256` is recorded, so that
# pin is NOT committed evidence -- see `RECAP_PHP.md` open item 13.
results-php/preflight/

# `.web/` — the static report over this tree's evidence. It was ignored here and
# kept its own local git history until it was folded into this repository. Its
# own `.web/.gitignore` still drops the derived (`data/`, which
# `.web/build_data.py` rebuilds in about a second) and the ephemeral.